    CHANGE-G2.md only accepts IDs that are already applied. "Not applied"
    covers unknown IDs too: an ID absent from the journal cannot be retained,
    and saying so here (`invalid-retain`) matters more than the later graph
    check, because a retention request the service silently ignored would
    drop changes the caller asked to keep.
